# A FIXED DEFECT, named after it (Go's `test/fixedbugs`).
#
# SYMPTOM (2026-08-11): `m["a"] @ "x" + "y"` printed `xy` and then
# `panic: 1 heap blocks still live at exit (a missing decref)`. Every answer
# correct, the failure at the sweep — the fourth time in this milestone.
#
# CAUSE: an indexed store hands the value OVER. `own.rs` increfs before it
# precisely so the primitive does not have to, which is why `hero_array_set`
# MOVES with `memcpy` and does not copy. `hero_map_set` copied through the value
# descriptor, increfing a second time. One leaked block per insert of a
# refcounted value.
#
# WHY NO TEST SAW IT: `run/maps.hero` uses `{str: i64}`, and an `i64`'s copy is a
# plain assignment — the double incref is invisible unless the VALUE owns a
# block. The cheaper spelling of the test passes.
# Bulk regression case.

function main()
    m: {str: str} @ {}
    m["a"] @ "x" + "y"
    m["a"] @ "z" + "w"
    print(m["a"].default("?"))
    print(len(m))
